# Issue #770, correction round 4. Every W6 capture carries the same set of artefact roles, and
# that set is a property of the campaign rather than of any document the campaign produces. It is
# declared here so the identity gate can require it from outside each document, the way
# MEASURED_CAPTURE_COUNT is required from outside. The producer builds a capture's provenance
# artefacts and its roles list from one collection, so a capture that under-reports its artefacts
# shortens both together and no cross-check inside the document can see it.
readonly EXPECTED_CAPTURE_ARTIFACT_ROLES='["AnnotatedPreview","Calibrated","Combined","Metadata","Preview","Raw"]'
# Issue #770, correction round 5. The role set alone anchors which roles a capture presents and
# not how many artefacts it presents for each, so a capture cut to one artefact per role kept all
# six roles and lost six hundred of nine hundred artefact digests without the gate objecting.
# This is the multiplicity, declared here rather than read out of the documents for the same
# reason MEASURED_CAPTURE_COUNT is. It is the histogram every one of the fifty captures in the
# five-trial campaign carries. Change it when the processing graph changes what a capture emits.
readonly EXPECTED_CAPTURE_ARTIFACT_ROLE_COUNTS='{"AnnotatedPreview":1,"Calibrated":1,"Combined":1,"Metadata":12,"Preview":2,"Raw":1}'

