# Issue #719. Two invocations over one durable root, named 'replay-719'. The first establishes the
# capture and replays it in process and retains the root; the second recreates only CameraAgent
# against that same root under LocalRunner, reads the first invocation's work out of durable state,
# and asserts the three-way output identity before deleting the root.
#
# The order is load-bearing and the pair is not separable. The second invocation is told nothing
# about the first: it finds the capture by requiring exactly one prior replay execution in the
# shared root. Running these in the other order, or either one alone, therefore fails outright
# rather than reporting a narrower pass.
#
# The capture counts are consumed only by the first invocation, which needs six captures to freeze
# a five-input rolling window. The second captures nothing; it is given the same numbers because
# the positional signature requires them, not because it uses them.
